:DEFAULT only supplies a fallback for a parameter of its scope. Defaulting
a :DECLAREd local fires diag.default_on_declare_line on the target name;
it is also misplaced, so diag.default_after_parameters fires on the same
statement (the two report different defects).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CountBins;
	:PARAMETERS sAisle;
	:DEFAULT sAisle, "A";
	:DECLARE nBins;
	:DEFAULT nBins, 0;
	nBins := Len(sAisle);
	:RETURN nBins;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CountBins;
	:PARAMETERS sAisle;
	:DEFAULT sAisle, "A";
	:DECLARE nBins;
	:DEFAULT nBins, 0;
	nBins := Len(sAisle);
	:RETURN nBins;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:2-5:10 error default_after_parameters: ':DEFAULT' must appear immediately after ':PARAMETERS'
5:11-5:16 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'nBins' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:2-5:10 error default_after_parameters: ':DEFAULT' must appear immediately after ':PARAMETERS'
5:11-5:16 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'nBins' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
